{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nCut the next minor release, 0.12.0, from reviewed main using docs/releasing.md. The current package and latest tag are 0.11.0/v0.11.0. PyPI is immutable; publication must use the dispatch-from-main workflow and its required pypi environment approval. The release date is 2026-08-15. Closed ticket reflective-sticky-grouper (9874-b1a9-2ff1-4cd3) is the 0.11.0 release precedent, not active duplicate work. CHANGELOG.md's [Unreleased] section already holds hand-curated entries, so per docs/releasing.md step 1a the changelog step is a retitle of [Unreleased] to [0.12.0] - 2026-08-15 (fresh empty [Unreleased] above it, compare links updated), not a make changelog regeneration.\n\n## Plan\n- Work in a fresh worktree based on current origin/main and confirm release prerequisites, identity, recent Gerrit history/rights, and channel state.\n- Bump pyproject.toml and every version in server.json to 0.12.0; regenerate uv.lock so the root project version remains locked at 0.12.0; retitle CHANGELOG.md's curated [Unreleased] section to [0.12.0] - 2026-08-15 with a fresh empty [Unreleased] and correct compare links.\n- Run version-lockstep and proportional release preflight: release-specific tests/guards, lock-currentness, lint, typecheck, full tests, build, and twine checks.\n- Commit with DCO, Change-Id, and rebar-ticket trailer; send through Gerrit and wait for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with no unresolved comments, then Submit.\n- After the bump lands on main, dispatch release.yml from main with version=0.12.0 and obtain the required pypi environment approval; monitor the entire workflow to a terminal result.\n- Verify PyPI 0.12.0 plus PEP 740 provenance, the v0.12.0 GitHub tag/release and artifacts, MCP Registry 0.12.0, and the Homebrew tap bump (trigger autobump if useful).\n- Install nava-rebar[mcp]==0.12.0 from PyPI in the distribution-channel environment and run the packaged post-publication probe.\n- Record receipts and results on this ticket, then close it only after all acceptance criteria are met.\n\n## File impact\n- pyproject.toml — package version bump\n- server.json — MCP manifest/package version bump\n- uv.lock — root package version lockstep with pyproject.toml\n- CHANGELOG.md — retitled curated 0.12.0 release section and compare links\n\n## Rollback / failure policy\nBefore publish, stop on any failed guard, review, or CI vote and remediate through a new Gerrit patchset. After publish, PyPI cannot be replaced: if the artifact is bad, yank 0.12.0, de-list its GitHub Release, and cut a fixed patch version; do not overwrite artifacts or retag published content.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] pyproject.toml declares version 0.12.0.\n- [ ] server.json top-level version is 0.12.0.\n- [ ] Every server.json packages[].version is 0.12.0.\n- [ ] uv.lock records the root nava-rebar package at version 0.12.0 and `uv lock --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md contains a hand-curated 0.12.0 section dated 2026-08-15.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md has a fresh Unreleased section and correct 0.12.0 compare links.\n- [ ] `python scripts/release_guards.py version-lockstep --version 0.12.0 --pyproject pyproject.toml --server-json server.json` exits 0.\n- [ ] Release-specific guard and workflow tests exit 0.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] `make test` exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] `python -m build` produces the 0.12.0 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ] `python -m twine check dist/*` exits 0 for the built artifacts.\n- [ ] The release commit contains DCO sign-off, a Gerrit Change-Id, and this rebar-ticket trailer.\n- [ ] Gerrit records LLM-Review +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit records Verified +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit has no unresolved comments on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit submits the release change and the resulting commit is on main.\n- [ ] release.yml is dispatched from main with version input 0.12.0.\n- [ ] The required pypi environment deployment is approved.\n- [ ] Every required release.yml job completes successfully.\n- [ ] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.12.0.\n- [ ] `uvx pypi-attestations verify pypi` on the published 0.12.0 wheel with --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar exits 0.\n- [ ] GitHub tag v0.12.0 resolves to the released main commit.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] GitHub Release v0.12.0 is marked Latest.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] GitHub Release v0.12.0 attaches the 0.12.0 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ] MCP Registry reports io.github.navapbc/rebar version 0.12.0.\n- [ ] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb points to the 0.12.0 PyPI sdist URL.\n- [ ] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb SHA-256 equals the PyPI 0.12.0 sdist digest.\n- [ ] A fresh channel install of nava-rebar[mcp]==0.12.0 passes scripts/probe_rebar.py with zero failures.\n- [ ] Release receipts, any exceptions, and the rollback disposition are recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786830183840139001,"uuid":"17aa6235-80c7-4771-a270-55b3f8340454"}